# Local context memory

At the start of a task, read `CONTEXT_MEMORY.txt` in the repo root if it exists. Treat it as the current project facts. Do not re-scan the repo for facts already recorded there.

When you learn or change something that the next session would otherwise have to rediscover (behavior, ports, model name, sizes, commands, user preferences), update `CONTEXT_MEMORY.txt` in the same turn. Keep it factual and short. Do not paste long code.

`CONTEXT_MEMORY.txt` is gitignored. Never stage it, commit it, or copy it into docs that are committed.
